  "title": "SUA: Fix trivial signed overflow",
  "description": "The literal 256 is an int. When multiplying it by a uint16_t, the\nunsigned short is promoted to an int by the integer promotions as\npart of the usual arithmetic conversions (because all values of\na uint16_t can be represented by an int.) This eventually can\noverflow, because what is wanted here is to combine two uint16_t\ninto a uint32_t.\n\nJust make them uint32_t to start with to prevent signed overflow.\nAlso go ahead and use proto_tree_add_item_ret_uint.\n\nOSS-Fuzz 458100286",
